<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Hudson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1565–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Hudson was an English navigator who searched for a northern sea route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Sailing for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in the Half <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> in 1609, he explored the river now named after him, opening the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> and New Netherland. On a voyage for English backers in 1610–1611 he entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a>, where his crew mutinied and set him adrift; he was never seen again.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-hudson.jpg" alt="Henry Hudson" width="320" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HenryHudson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
